WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.020
Give SpecWithCode one goal.

2
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.080
Its coordinator hands each piece of work to a thread.

3
00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:10.400
A thread keeps its context,

4
00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:13.810
so a follow-up goes back to the thread that already knows the work.

5
00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:17.700
Claude Code, Codex and other agents work in parallel,

6
00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:19.900
on your own machines.

7
00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:22.700
Then you review one result.

8
00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:25.700
When one agent hits a usage limit,

9
00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.350
the same thread continues on another.

10
00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:31.200
Agents can even use your own Chrome,

11
00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.980
with the SpecWithCode Browser extension.

12
00:00:35.150 --> 00:00:39.790
SpecWithCode is a free download for macOS, Windows and Linux.

13
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.720
At spec-weave.com/code.
